.TH LEAKCHECK 1 "2026" "leakcheck 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
leakcheck \- find memory bugs, leaked resources, weak source and malware in C and C++ programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B leakcheck
.I mode
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.RI [ target-args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B leakcheck
has three independent modes that share one reporter, so the console, JSON and
SARIF output and the exit status are the same from each.
.TP
.B dynamic
Runs the program with a tracking library loaded into it and reports what
actually happened: leaks, double frees, use after free, overflows, leaked
descriptors and processes, deadlocks, and what a trojan does to the machine.
The program is executed; run untrusted programs in a virtual machine.
.TP
.B static
Parses C and C++ sources and follows pointers, handles and locks through each
function, and reads the source for weaknesses such as format strings, command
injection, unbounded copies, hard-coded secrets and check-then-use races. There
is no compiler front end, so it runs anywhere in milliseconds and is tuned for
few false alarms rather than completeness.
.TP
.B scan
Reads files and folders for signs of malware without executing anything.
.TP
.B ai-features
Prints the numbers
.B scan --ai
reads from each Windows program. It exists for training the classifier.
.SH OPTIONS
Options go before the target. In dynamic mode everything after the program is
passed to it unchanged.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIfile\fR
Write the report to \fIfile\fR instead of standard output. Required for
\fB\-f json\fR and \fB\-f sarif\fR in dynamic mode.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIconsole|json|sarif\fR
Output format. The default is \fBconsole\fR; \fBsarif\fR is SARIF 2.1.0 for
code-scanning services.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-suppressions " " \fIfile\fR
Ignore findings matching rules written as \fItype\fR:\fIpattern\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-error\-exitcode " " \fIn\fR
Exit status when problems are found, 1 to 255. The default is 2.
.TP
.B \-\-malware
Also look for the 100 malware families, in files, in source and in what the
program does. Much slower; off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-ai
In scan mode, also ask the trained classifier about every Windows program.
Needs \fImodel/pe\-malware.ai\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-ai\-model " " \fIfile\fR ", " \-\-ai\-threshold " " \fI0..1\fR
Use another model, or another score above which a file counts as malware.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIn\fR
Files read at the same time, for scan, static and ai-features. The default is
one per CPU; the report is identical for any number.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version, the commit it was built from, the build type and the
classifier it would use.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the full option list, including the dynamic-mode options
(\fB\-\-guard\-every\fR, \fB\-\-quarantine\-mb\fR, \fB\-\-stack\-depth\fR,
\fB\-\-fast\-unwind\fR, \fB\-\-abort\-on\-error\fR, \fB\-\-trace\-children\fR,
\fB\-\-show\-reachable\fR, \fB\-\-no\-leak\-check\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 2
Something was found (change with \fB\-\-error\-exitcode\fR).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, or nothing could be analysed.
.TP
.B 0
Clean. In dynamic mode the program's own status is returned instead, and
\fB127\fR when it could not be started.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I model/pe\-malware.ai
The shipped classifier, found next to the binary, next to the project root, or
under \fIshare/leakcheck/model\fR.
.TP
.I libleakcheck_preload.so
The runtime injected in dynamic mode. On Windows,
\fIleakcheck_preload.dll\fR. It must stay beside the \fBleakcheck\fR binary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
leakcheck dynamic ./my_program arg1
leakcheck static src/ \-f sarif \-o leakcheck.sarif
leakcheck scan ./downloads/
leakcheck scan \-\-ai ./downloads/ \-f json \-o scan.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The full reference, the design notes and the model description are installed
under \fIshare/doc/leakcheck\fR and kept in the source tree under \fIdocs/\fR.
